{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.RepresentationTheory","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.RepresentationTheory","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Glossary","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse","lean:module:QOU.KnotTheory","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Functor.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.NatTrans","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Factorial.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Combinatorics.Young.YoungDiagram","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":48,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.clebsch_gordan_fundamental","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.clebsch_gordan_fundamental","kind":"theorem","line":294,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L294-L303","doc":"The Clebsch–Gordan decomposition: `V_{1/2} ⊗ V_{1/2} ≅ V_0 ⊕ V_1`.\nIn terms of categorical dimensions: `dim(V_{1/2})² = dim(V_0) + dim(V_1)`,\ni.e. `2 · 2 = 1 + 3`.  Generic over any monoidal category `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.hadron_tensor_factorization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.hadron_tensor_factorization","kind":"theorem","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L271-L292","doc":"A categorical hadron factors through tensor powers of `V` via\nthe PawLei embedding.  Each constituent `V_{j_i}` embeds into\n`V_{1/2}^⊗(2j_i)`, so the full hadron embeds into\n`V_{1/2}^⊗(2(j_1 + ⋯ + j_n))`.\n\nThe hypothesis `spins_pos` ensures all constituents have nonzero\nspin (spin-0 is the trivial representation, which contributes\nnothing to the tensor embedding).\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{rem:knot-factorization}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.pawLei_orthogonal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.pawLei_orthogonal","kind":"theorem","line":261,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L261-L267","doc":"Orthogonality: the PL inner product of distinct basis vectors vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PawLeiOrthogonalIP.orthogonal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PawLeiOrthogonalIP.orthogonal","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L259-L259","doc":"Off-diagonal entries vanish (orthogonality). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PawLeiOrthogonalIP.diagonal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PawLeiOrthogonalIP.diagonal","kind":"theorem","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L257-L257","doc":"Diagonal entries equal the norm squared. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PawLeiOrthogonalIP.innerProduct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PawLeiOrthogonalIP.innerProduct","kind":"def","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L254-L254","doc":"The inner product function. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PawLeiOrthogonalIP.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PawLeiOrthogonalIP.mk","kind":"ctor","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L252-L252","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PawLeiOrthogonalIP.toPawLeiInnerProduct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PawLeiOrthogonalIP.toPawLeiInnerProduct","kind":"def","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L252-L259","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PawLeiOrthogonalIP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PawLeiOrthogonalIP","kind":"structure","line":248,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L248-L259","doc":"The **orthogonal inner product** induced by the PL basis.\nThe adjoint trace defines a bilinear form on intertwiner spaces that\nis diagonal in the PL basis: `⟨T_λ, T_μ⟩_PL = δ_{λμ} ‖T_λ‖²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PawLeiInnerProduct.normSq_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PawLeiInnerProduct.normSq_pos","kind":"theorem","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L246-L246","doc":"All norms are positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PawLeiInnerProduct.normSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PawLeiInnerProduct.normSq","kind":"def","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L243-L243","doc":"The norm-squared of each basis vector (positive rational). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PawLeiInnerProduct.basis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PawLeiInnerProduct.basis","kind":"def","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L241-L241","doc":"The underlying basis data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PawLeiInnerProduct.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PawLeiInnerProduct.mk","kind":"ctor","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L239-L239","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PawLeiInnerProduct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PawLeiInnerProduct","kind":"structure","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L229-L246","doc":"The **Pawlowski–Leitner inner product** on intertwiner spaces.\n\nDefined via the adjoint trace:\n`⟨φ, ψ⟩_PL = tr_Ad(φ† ∘ ψ) = λ ∘ μ ∘ (φ† ∘ ψ ⊗ id) ∘ coev_{V_j}`\n\nThe Pawlowski–Leitner basis `{T_λ}` is orthogonal with respect to\nthis pairing: `⟨T_λ, T_μ⟩_PL = δ_{λμ} ‖T_λ‖²`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:pawlowski-leitner-inner-product}`\nRef: [leitnerpawloski2004] PL inner product / intertwiner basis (arXiv:math/0409565) ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:pawlowski-leitner-inner-product","label":"prop:pawlowski-leitner-inner-product","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/pawlowski-leitner-inner-product.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PawLeiBasis.num_basis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PawLeiBasis.num_basis","kind":"def","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L225-L225","doc":"The number of basis elements equals the intertwiner dimension. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PawLeiBasis.n_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PawLeiBasis.n_ge","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L223-L223","doc":"The tensor power is large enough: `n ≥ 2j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PawLeiBasis.parity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PawLeiBasis.parity","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L221-L221","doc":"Parity constraint: `n ≡ 2j (mod 2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PawLeiBasis.n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PawLeiBasis.n","kind":"def","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L219-L219","doc":"The tensor power. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PawLeiBasis.twice_j","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PawLeiBasis.twice_j","kind":"def","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L217-L217","doc":"The spin label (as twice_j). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PawLeiBasis.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PawLeiBasis.mk","kind":"ctor","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L215-L215","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PawLeiBasis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PawLeiBasis","kind":"structure","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L209-L225","doc":"The **Pawlowski–Leitner basis** for the intertwiner space\n`Hom_{SU(2)}(V_j, V_{1/2}^⊗n)` is indexed by standard Young\ntableaux of shape `λ ⊢ n` with at most 2 rows and\n`λ₁ - λ₂ = 2j`.\n\nRef: [leitnerpawloski2004] PL inner product / intertwiner basis (arXiv:math/0409565) ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:pawlowski-leitner-basis","label":"prop:pawlowski-leitner-basis","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/pawlowski-leitner-basis.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.pawLei_minimal_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.pawLei_minimal_dim","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L196-L207","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.pawLeiDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.pawLeiDim","kind":"def","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L174-L188","doc":"The **dimension of the intertwiner space**\n`Hom_{SU(2)}(V_j, V_{1/2}^⊗n)`.\n\nGiven by the hook-length formula:\n`dim = (2j+1) · n! / ((n/2 + j + 1)! · (n/2 - j)!)`\nwhen `n ≡ 2j (mod 2)` and `n ≥ 2j`, and zero otherwise.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:pawlowski-leitner-basis}`\nRef: [leitnerpawloski2004] PL inner product / intertwiner basis (arXiv:math/0409565) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.killingFormRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.killingFormRatio","kind":"def","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L168-L170","doc":"The Killing form ratio: in SU(2), `tr_Ad = -2 · tr_{ℂ²}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AdjointTrace.fundamentalObj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AdjointTrace.fundamentalObj","kind":"def","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L166-L166","doc":"The fundamental object `V` on which endomorphisms are traced. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AdjointTrace.frobHopf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AdjointTrace.frobHopf","kind":"def","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L164-L164","doc":"The Frobenius–Hopf data providing the trace infrastructure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AdjointTrace.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AdjointTrace.mk","kind":"ctor","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L161-L161","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AdjointTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AdjointTrace","kind":"structure","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L147-L166","doc":"The **adjoint trace** on endomorphisms of `V`.\n\nGiven a Frobenius–Hopf data `(A, μ, η, Δ, ε, λ)`, the adjoint\ntrace of an endomorphism `f : V → V` is defined as\n`tr_Ad(f) = λ ∘ μ ∘ (f ⊗ id_{V∨}) ∘ coev_V`.\n\nProperties:\n- Cyclicity: `tr_Ad(f ∘ g) = tr_Ad(g ∘ f)`\n- Non-degeneracy: `⟨f, g⟩_Ad = tr_Ad(f† ∘ g)` is non-degenerate\n\nIn the archimedean realisation with `G = SU(2)`, this recovers the\nKilling form: `tr_Ad(f) = -2 tr_{ℂ²}(f)`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{rem:adjoint-trace}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalHadron.totalTensorPower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalHadron.totalTensorPower","kind":"def","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L138-L143","doc":"The total tensor power needed to embed a categorical hadron into\n`V^⊗N` via the Pawlowski–Leitner embedding: `N = 2(j₁ + ⋯ + jₙ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.meson_or_baryon_or_exotic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.meson_or_baryon_or_exotic","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L129-L136","doc":"Every categorical hadron is a meson, baryon, or exotic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalHadron.isMeson","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalHadron.isMeson","kind":"def","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L124-L127","doc":"A categorical meson has valence 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalHadron.isBaryon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalHadron.isBaryon","kind":"def","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L119-L122","doc":"A categorical baryon has valence 3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalHadron.constituent_spins","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalHadron.constituent_spins","kind":"def","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L117-L117","doc":"The spin labels of the constituents (each as twice_j). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalHadron.valence_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalHadron.valence_ge","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L115-L115","doc":"Valence is at least 2 (at least two constituents). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalHadron.valence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalHadron.valence","kind":"def","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L113-L113","doc":"The valence: number of constituent simple objects. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalHadron.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalHadron.mk","kind":"ctor","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L110-L110","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalHadron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalHadron","kind":"structure","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L101-L117","doc":"A **categorical hadron** is a morphism `𝟙 → V^⊗n` for some `n ≥ 2`,\nrepresenting a composite particle as a tensor product of fundamental\nobjects.  The morphism factors through the Frobenius comultiplication\nand projections to simple summands.\n\nThis is the purely categorical predecessor of the localized hadron\n(`def:hadron`) which adds a base point on the projective line.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:categorical-hadron}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.trivial_is_spin_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.trivial_is_spin_zero","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L94-L97","doc":"The trivial object corresponds to spin 0 (twice_j = 0). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.adjoint_is_spin_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.adjoint_is_spin_one","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L89-L92","doc":"The adjoint object corresponds to spin 1 (twice_j = 2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.fundamental_is_spin_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.fundamental_is_spin_half","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L84-L87","doc":"The fundamental object corresponds to spin 1/2 (twice_j = 1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.spinSimpleObject","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.spinSimpleObject","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L75-L82","doc":"Spin-indexed simple objects: `V_j` has categorical dimension `2j + 1`,\nwhere `j` is represented as `twice_j / 2` (so `twice_j` is a natural\nnumber). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.adjointSimpleObject","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.adjointSimpleObject","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L68-L73","doc":"The adjoint simple object: categorical dimension 3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.fundamentalSimpleObject","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.fundamentalSimpleObject","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L56-L66","doc":"The fundamental object `V`: the unique simple object of categorical\ndimension 2.  Every other simple object `V_j` appears as a direct\nsummand of some tensor power `V^⊗n`, so `V` generates `C` as a\ntensor category.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{rem:simple-objects-V}`, `\\label{rem:fundamental-object-explication}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SimpleObject.catDim_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SimpleObject.catDim_pos","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L54-L54","doc":"The categorical dimension is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SimpleObject.catDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SimpleObject.catDim","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L52-L52","doc":"The categorical dimension (rank of `τ(obj)` as a free R-module). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SimpleObject.obj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SimpleObject.obj","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L50-L50","doc":"The underlying object in `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SimpleObject.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SimpleObject.mk","kind":"ctor","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SimpleObject","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SimpleObject","kind":"structure","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/RepresentationTheory.lean#L40-L54","doc":"An object `X` in a monoidal category `C` is **simple** if every\nmonomorphism into `X` is either zero or an isomorphism.\n\nWhen the fibre functor `τ` is faithful and exact, `X` is simple in\n`C` iff `τ(X)` is a simple (irreducible) module.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{rem:simple-objects-V}` ","signatureChunk":0}]}